{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1097396-around-the-world-in-80-ways-the-gallain","id":1097396,"title":"Around the World in 80 Ways: the Gallain","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Changeling: The Dreaming"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-05-26T19:39:58-07:00","id":1097396,"title":"<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/icons/icon1.png\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" alt=\"\" /> Around the World in 80 Ways: the Gallain","content":"This thread is intended for house rules for the Gallain. Before we get started, we should probably clarify just what the Gallain <i>are</i>. The Gallain are changelings who use a different paradigm than the Kithain, usually culture-based. They have their own Kiths and Houses, and can potentially change any other aspects of changeling nature. In the context of the Gallain, the Kithain can be thought of as \u201cmerely\u201d another kind of Gallain; this is emphasized in the write-up of the Fae Realm, which stresses that it should be contextualized.<br /> <br /> The published Gallain are:<br /> \u00b7 The Nunnehi: changelings native to North America.<br /> \u00b7 The Menehuni: changelings native to Hawaii.<br /> \u00b7 The Hsien: changelings native to Japan.<br /> \u00b7 The Inanimae: changelings tied to the elements.<br /> <br /> And the Kithain are changelings native to Western and Central Europe and Northern Africa. <br /> <br /> More Gallain can be conceived, such as Djinni of the Middle East. <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-26T22:34:31-07:00","id":1097426,"title":"","content":"The Hsien are SE Asia in general, its why most of them have chinese Names.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-27T00:12:00-07:00","id":1097443,"title":"","content":"Djinni I believe is the Singular, and Djinn is plural, I often get them confused.<br /> <br /> <br /> But I say Merfolk are Gallain, as they were in previous editions. They are born from eggs at the bottom of the see for goshsake! So that seems to also indicate there communities are the largest Fae Communities since they are born from breeding with themselves, or getting preggo from drunk Sailors.<br /> <br /> You can change houses right? Because I wonder the idea of Merfolk joining Kithain Houses, or Kithain joining the Merfolk.<br /> <br /> But I can't see how they are Kithain. They are not born of the Changeling Way Ritual as the Kithain know it, and they are children of Vatea, rather then the Tuatha. They also are extra hidden as they were often thought to be just a myth to the Kithain, who themselves are thought to be just a myth to the other Supernaturals.<br /> <br /> <br /> Also I wonder if the Hsien are Gallain at all rather then Prodigals. If they are they are more tied to Dark Age Fae, their ancestors not being tied to the Dreaming but the Beings the Fae were before they retreated to the World. Their Past Lives having bent to Heavens whim. Did C20 tie them closer to the Changelings? Because from my understanding since they aren't tied to the Dreaming they wouldn't see a Changelings Fae Mien, and vice versa. And does that mean the Dreaming of Asia is more primordial being mostly untouched without native changelings. Making Inanimae the closest shepards of Dreams for most of history, and Adhene recently (They came after the Week of Nightmares right? Or were they always active?), though maybe Adhene are in greater number in Asia, there are plenty of stories of Possession after all. Makes me think they should have a Baku Adhene.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-27T00:26:41-07:00","id":1097444,"title":"","content":"TV Tropes mentioned, that some fans made Djinn kiths. Anybody knows?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>...","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5211-firkraag","name":"Firkraag","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5211_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"381"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-27T00:44:53-07:00","id":1097448,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Firkraag</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1097396-around-the-world-in-80-ways-the-gallain?p=1097444#post1097444\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">TV Tropes mentioned, that some fans made Djinn kiths. Anybody knows?</div> </div> </div> </div>There was definitely a project going on SnE for those. I think it was called 'The Smokeless Fire'?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3959-urabyfirst","name":"Urabyfirst","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"43"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-30T17:44:41-07:00","id":1098625,"title":"","content":"Shadowessence took a lot of Changeling material with it: the most relevant to me is the Asura project (India).<br /> Not only did we get new a new breed of Gallain, but we got new Adhene (commonly referred to as Dark-Kin, but honestly i feel like the are closer to what pre-Shattering fae) and a new take on the Inanimae.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thoughts ripple out, birthing others","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","name":"FallenEco","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1927"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-05T17:34:19-07:00","id":1100655,"title":"","content":"Hsien don't appear to be related in any way to other Changelings. Nothing about them says so. Their method of reincarnation is different, their powers are different, their relationship with the Dreaming and the Umbra is different. Honestly, there as much Kithain and the Kuei-Jin are Kindred. There's a vague resemblance and that is it. I know many who feel that marketing the Hsien as a Changeling product did neither game justice.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3988-windthin","name":"Windthin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3988_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"126"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-05T18:53:27-07:00","id":1100675,"title":"","content":"I definitely consider the Hsien to be pushing the envelope in terms of how much the Gallain can differ from the Kithain. That said, they're in C20, so I'm not going to argue that they should be completely segregated from Changeling. Rather, I'd be more interested, for the purpose of this thread, in ideas for how to bridge the gap between Hsien and Kithain. My thought is to introduce other Gallain that exist in the space between the two. In a sense, the Menehuni and Nunnehi already do (in that both tend to be more interested in the spirit world than in the Dreaming), though they're arguably much closer to Kithain than to Hsien. But maybe there could be other Far East Gallain that are to the Hsien as the Nunnehi are to the Kithain\u2026<br /> <br /> On that note, here's something I found in the archives for B.J.Zanzibar's World of Darkness: a Japanese Gallain called the <a href=\"http://bjz-backup.droppages.com/archive/sei.html\" target=\"_blank\">Sei</a>: Oni, Kappa, Tengu (<i>not</i> Eastern Corax), and Hengeyokai (think more along the lines of Pooka: trickster animals, including but not limited to foxes and tanuki). This could be used as a baseline for an expansion on or alternative to the Hsien.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":421,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","user":"Dataweaver","date":". 06-05-2017, 11:12 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-05T20:24:40-07:00","id":1100685,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>FallenEco</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1097396-around-the-world-in-80-ways-the-gallain?p=1098625#post1098625\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Shadowessence took a lot of Changeling material with it: the most relevant to me is the Asura project (India).<br /> Not only did we get new a new breed of Gallain, but we got new Adhene (commonly referred to as Dark-Kin, but honestly i feel like the are closer to what pre-Shattering fae) and a new take on the Inanimae.</div> </div> </div> </div>Shadownessence is lost to the Mists; but B.J.Zanzibar's World of Darkness has the <a href=\"http://bjz-backup.droppages.com/archive/pari.html\" target=\"_blank\">Pari</a>; there might be something useful there.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-08T05:50:07-07:00","id":1101590,"title":"","content":"I rather prefer the idea that the Hsien are not fae at all, to be honest. I like the fact that there are other types of beings NOT necessarily Eurocentric. I've always wanted to see something unique coming out of Africa or the Americas, on that note.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3988-windthin","name":"Windthin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3988_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"126"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-09T17:02:48-07:00","id":1102151,"title":"","content":"Just because Changeling calls it &quot;fae&quot; doesn't mean that it's Eurocentric, or even all that much like the European fae. That's kind of what I was getting at when I was talking about there being a spectrum of Gallain, with the Hsien representing a particularly extreme example of how much the Gallain can potentially differ from the Kithain. Contrast them with <a href=\"http://bjz-backup.droppages.com/archive/hengeyokai_kith.html\" target=\"_blank\">Colin Chapman's Hengeyokai</a>, which I'd cite as an example of how to do the same concept in a manner much closer to how the Kithain work.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-13T10:04:30-07:00","id":1103180,"title":"","content":"You say \u201cthey have no reason to be more likely to encounter or interact with changelings than with any other supernatural.\u201d Would it be sufficient to say that they're aware of and interact with Chimerical Reality, and are otherwise exactly like they're portrayed in <b>Land of Eight Million Dreams</b>? If that's not sufficient, what more needs to be done?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-13T20:05:54-07:00","id":1103365,"title":"","content":"I didn't read c20 yet, so hsien can see Fae miens and chimera now?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}